  "recommended_integration": [
    "Extend the existing seven-arm matched CPU table with Citation2 edge and edge + DRNL columns, preserving graph-specific cohort denominators.",
    "Persistent native has the lowest aggregate time in both matched cohorts; Citation2 full-clear and direct overheads are much smaller than on Friendster.",
    "Citation2 aggregate scan time is lower than pair probing, illustrating a second workload regime without a universal winning Numba plan.",
    "Include conversion, map bytes and one-time initialization separately. Retain repeated-cache, unpinned-affinity and differing low-level output-materialization caveats."
  ],
  "claim_limits": [
    "128 cases are not 128 independent queries: Friendster reuses 90 distinct physical pairs; Citation2 reuses 80 pairs and 126 distinct ordered sets.",
    "No population confidence interval, language superiority, end-to-end/first-batch speedup, quality or new PSS claim.",
    "Cross-graph differences are descriptive; graph size alone is not isolated as their cause.",
    "E22 is a new separately audited experiment and does not retroactively modify the published v0.5.0 artifact."
  ]
